# Copy to .env and adjust. Never commit .env.

NODE_ENV=development
PORT=4000
HOST=0.0.0.0

# ── MongoDB. `./scripts/dev-up.sh` sets all of this up for you; these are the
# values it uses, written down so a manual run is possible.
#
# A REPLICA SET IS MANDATORY. The gapless chain appender is a compare-and-swap
# inside a transaction, transactions need a replica set, and the API refuses to
# start against a standalone mongod. A single node is fine for development.
#
#   docker run -d --name pramaan-mongo -p 27018:27018 mongo:7 \
#     mongod --replSet rs0 --port 27018
#   docker exec pramaan-mongo mongosh --port 27018 --eval 'rs.initiate()'
#
# ⚠ THE PORT MAPPING MUST MATCH ON BOTH SIDES. `-p 27018:27017` fails with
# ReplicaSetNoPrimary, because a replica set advertises its own host:port and the
# driver then reconnects to the port it was told about, not the one you mapped.
#
# ⚠ Wait for a PRIMARY, not just a listening port. The election takes a moment
# after rs.initiate(), and starting the API too early fails in a way that reads
# like a bad connection string.
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://127.0.0.1:27018/?replicaSet=rs0
MONGODB_DB=pramaan

# Atlas. Leave MONGODB_URI pointing at the local replica set so the default path
# never depends on the cloud; set this and pass it explicitly to migrate or test:
#   MONGODB_URI="$ATLAS_URI" npm run db:migrate
# ⚠ Atlas is UNTESTED as of 14 Aug 2026, and reaching it makes D-25, D-26 and
# NFR-6 inaccurate — MongoDB Inc joins the trusted set and Atlas becomes a
# sub-processor no agreement names. D-3 carries that as a gate on this step.
# ATLAS_URI=

# ── MySQL is LEGACY. Nothing in src/ may import it. These are needed only by
# apps/api/tools/migrate-to-mongo.mjs, to read an old chain across, and the whole
# set should be deleted together once the MySQL data is confirmed unneeded.
# DB_HOST=127.0.0.1
# DB_PORT=3307
# DB_USER=pramaan
# DB_PASSWORD=pramaan
# DB_NAME=pramaan

# Production refuses to start with the dev fallback.
JWT_SECRET=dev-only-do-not-use-in-production
JWT_EXPIRES_IN=30d

# ── The chain signing key. This is what makes every record in the evidence chain
# attributable to this server, so .data/ is gitignored and the key is never
# committed. In production config.js THROWS if this is unset, deliberately: the
# key must be at a known path and backed up, not silently regenerated somewhere
# ephemeral — a lost key cannot verify any record signed with it.
CHAIN_KEY_PATH=.data/chain-signing-key.pem
CHAIN_HEADS_FILE=.data/published-heads.jsonl
CHAIN_MAX_BATCH=500

OTP_TTL_MINUTES=10
OTP_MAX_ATTEMPTS=5
# "log" prints the code instead of sending an SMS. Production refuses this.
# O-5 (notification transport) is open and has a weeks-long lead time.
OTP_DELIVERY=log

# White-label by configuration, never a code fork. FRD NFR-7.
BRAND_NAME=Pramaan
CONTRACTOR_NAME=Demo Contractor

CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000
